": "MSFT", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2022", "period_end": "2022-06-30", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.8848, "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-K FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000156459022026876/msft-10k_20220630.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2022-06-30__mdna__0019", "ticker": "MSFT", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2022", "period_end": "2022-06-30", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.8481, "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-K FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000156459022026876/msft-10k_20220630.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10Q_2022-03-31__mdna__0026", "ticker": "MSFT", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q3 FY2022", "period_end": "2022-03-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.8207, "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-Q Q3 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000156459022015675/msft-10q_20220331.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10Q_2022-03-31__mdna__0025", "ticker": "MSFT", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q3 FY2022", "period_end": "2022-03-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.7568, "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-Q Q3 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000156459022015675/msft-10q_20220331.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10Q_2022-03-31__financial_statements__0098", "ticker": "MSFT", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q3 FY2022", "period_end": "2022-03-31", "section": "financial_statements", "score": 0.7193, "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-Q Q3 FY2022", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000156459022015675/msft-10q_20220331.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 36, "dropped_candidates": 71, "token_estimate": 30944, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "Microsoft says it operates and reports its financial performance using three segments: Productivity and Business Processes, Intelligent Cloud, and More Personal Computing [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0003]. It states the segments give management a comprehensive financial view of its key businesses and provide a framework for allocating resources [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0003]. Productivity and Business Processes covers productivity, communication, and information services, Intelligent Cloud covers public, private, and hybrid server products and cloud services, and More Personal Computing covers products and services that put customers at the center of the experience [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__financial_statements__0124] [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__financial_statements__0125]. In August 2024 Microsoft announced changes to segment composition, most notably bringing the commercial components of Microsoft 365 together in Productivity and Business Processes, effective in fiscal 2025, ended June 30, 2025 [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__mdna__0004]. The three-segment structure and the segment definitions are carried through the latest filing, Q2 fiscal 2026, ended December 31, 2025 [MSFT_10Q_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0089].", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "MSFT", "company": "Microsoft Corporation", "findings": [{"point": "Productivity and Business Processes primarily comprises Microsoft 365 Commercial and Consumer products and cloud services, LinkedIn, and Dynamics products and cloud services (fiscal 2025, ended June 30, 2025).", "citations": ["MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__financial_statements__0124"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Intelligent Cloud primarily comprises Server products and cloud services (including Azure, GitHub, and Nuance Healthcare cloud services) and Enterprise and partner services (fiscal 2025, ended June 30, 2025).", "citations": ["MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__financial_statements__0124"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "More Personal Computing primarily comprises Windows and Devices, Gaming, and Search and news advertising (fiscal 2025, ended June 30, 2025).", "citations": ["MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__financial_statements__0125"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": {"columns": ["Segment", "How Microsoft describes it (fiscal 2025, ended June 30, 2025)"], "rows": [["Productivity and Business Processes", "Productivity, communication, and information services across devices and platforms [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__financial_statements__0124]"], ["Intelligent Cloud", "Public, private, and hybrid server products and cloud services for business and developers [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__financial_statements__0124]"], ["More Personal Computing", "Products and services that put customers at the center of the experience [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__financial_statements__0125]"]]}, "citations": [{"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0003", "claim": "Three segments; purpose of segments", "quote": "We operate our business and report our financial performance using three segments"}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__financial_statements__0124", "claim": "Productivity and Intelligent Cloud definitions", "quote": "Our Intelligent Cloud segment consists of our public, private, and hybrid server products and cloud services"}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__financial_statements__0125", "claim": "More Personal Computing definition", "quote": "Our More Personal Computing segment consists of products and services that put customers at the center of the experience"}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__mdna__0004", "claim": "August 2024 segment composition change", "quote": "bringing the commercial components of Microsoft 365 together in the Productivity and Business Processes segment"}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10Q_2025-12-31__financial_statements__0089", "claim": "Segments unchanged in latest 10-Q", "quote": "we reported our financial performance based on the following segments: Productivity and Business Processes, Intelligent Cloud, and More Personal Computing"}], "coverage": {"companies_used": [{"ticker": "MSFT", "forms": ["10-K", "10-Q"], "fiscal_periods": ["FY2025", "Q2 FY2026"]}], "companies_missing": [], "data_as_of": "Q2 FY2026, ended December 31, 2025 (filed 2026-01-28)"}, "gaps": ["The answer centers on fiscal 2025 and Q2 fiscal 2026 wording; earlier filings (fiscal 2022 to fiscal 2024) describe segment contents differently (for example Office Commercial and Windows in More Personal Computing) and are not detailed here.", "Segment revenue and operating income figures were not requested and are not discussed."], "confidence": "high", "confidence_reason": "Multiple filings state the three-segment structure and segment descriptions consistently, with the most recent 10-K and 10-Q directly quoted.", "next_questions": ["How did segment revenue and operating income change in fiscal 2025, ended June 30, 2025?", "How did the August 2024 segment recast change what sits in each segment?", "How does Microsoft allocate shared revenue and costs among segments?"], "refusal": null}, "citations_resolved": [{"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__business__0003", "claim": "Three segments; purpose of segments", "quote": "We operate our business and report our financial performance using three segments", "ticker": "MSFT", "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-K FY2025", "section_title": "Business", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-06-30", "filing_date": "2025-07-30", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/000095017025100235/msft-20250630.htm", "truncated": false, "quote_mismatch": false, "valid": true, "kind": "chunk"}, {"chunk_id": "MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__financial_statements__0124", "claim": "Productivity and Intelligent Cloud definitions", "quote": "Our Intelligent Cloud segment consists of our public, private, and hybrid server products and cloud services", "ticker": "MSFT", "filing_name": "Microsoft Corporation 10-K FY2025", "section_title": "Financial Statements", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-06-30", "filing_date": "2025-07-30", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/789019/0000950170